{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-33860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,1-3t,\\,5+6t⟩$, $t\\ge 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=7t.$ Find $R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s=7t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{7}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s$, with $s\\ge 0$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{7}) \\\\  & =⟨2(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,1-3(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,5+6(\\frac{s}{7})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-33860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,1-3s,\\,5+6s⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7+3s,\\,35+6s⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨2s,\\,7+3s,\\,35+6s⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve $r(t)=3t\\,i+2{t}^{3/2}\\,j+4\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by  $s=2(1+t)^{3/2}-2.$ Given that $R(s)$ is the parameterization of the given curve by its arc length $s,$ what is the $y$-component of $R?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s=2(1+t)^{3/2}-2$, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =2(1+t)^{3/2}-2 \\\\ s+2 & =2(1+t)^{3/2} \\\\ \\frac{s+2}{2} & =(1+t)^{3/2} \\\\ {(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3} & =1+t \\\\ t & ={(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r({(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1) \\\\  & =3[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1]\\,i+2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}\\,j+4\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the $y$-component of $R$ is\n\n$$\n2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-33978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{1/3}-1]}^{3/2}"] ["math" "2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}"] ["math" "2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}-1)}^{1/3}+1]}^{3/2}"] ["math" "3{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{3/2}"] ["math" "{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{3/2}-1]}^{3/2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127687" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve $r(t)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s={e}^{t}-1.$ Given that $R(s)$ is the parametrization of the given curve by its arc length $s,$ what is the $x$-component of $R?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127687" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s={e}^{t}-1,$ we have that $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1).$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the $x$-component of $R$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127687" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-127687" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127687" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s)]"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s+1)"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}s\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s)]"] ["math" "s\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127687" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=6t.$ Find $R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s=6t,$ we have that $t=\\frac{s}{6}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{6}) \\\\  & =⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{s}{6}),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{s}{6})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-127689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2s),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2s)⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3s+2),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3s+2)⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3s-6),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3s-6)⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-34885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve$r(t)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))\\,j,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by  $s=4t.$ Find $R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-34885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s=4t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{4}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s$, with $s\\ge 0$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{4}) \\\\  & =(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{4}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{4}))\\,j \\\\  & =(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-34885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-34885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-34885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2s))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2s))\\,j"] ["math" "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8s))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8s))\\,j"] ["math" "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+(2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,j"] ["math" "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,j"] ["math" "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-34885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve  $r(t)=⟨2{e}^{t},\\,3{e}^{t},\\,6{e}^{t}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=7({e}^{t}-1),$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s=7({e}^{t}-1)$, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{s}{7} & ={e}^{t}-1 \\\\ {e}^{t} & =\\frac{s}{7}+1 \\\\ t & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})) \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})},\\,3{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})},\\,6{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\cdot \\frac{s+7}{7},\\,3\\cdot \\frac{s+7}{7},\\,6\\cdot \\frac{s+7}{7}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2s+14}{7},\\,\\frac{3s+21}{7},\\,\\frac{6s+42}{7}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2s+14}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3s+21}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{6s+42}{7})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7},\\,\\frac{6}{7}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-78403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{7},\\,\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{14},\\,\\frac{3}{14},\\,\\frac{2}{7}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\frac{6}{5}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7},\\,\\frac{6}{7}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7},\\,\\frac{6}{7}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve  $r(t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6t\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=10t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s=10t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{10}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{10}) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+6(\\frac{s}{10})k \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3s}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{s}{10})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3s}{5})k \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+8\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-33861" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33861" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "T(s)=-80\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+80\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "T(s)=-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10s)\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10s)\\,j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "T(s)=-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "T(s)=80\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i-80\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33861" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "T(s)=-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=8t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡6t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡6t\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=10t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s=10t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{10}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{10}) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{s}{10})\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6s}{10})j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6s}{10})k \\\\  & =\\frac{4s}{5}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4s}{5})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5}))j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5}))k \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-33984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "T(s)=\\frac{2s}{5}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{4s}{5}\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{4s}{5}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-33984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "T(s)=\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve  $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{2},\\,8{t}^{2}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=9{t}^{2},$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s=9{t}^{2}$, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{s}{9} \\\\ t & =\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨{(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3})}^{2},\\,4{(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3})}^{2},\\,8{(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3})}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{s}{9},\\,\\frac{4s}{9},\\,\\frac{8s}{9}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{9}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4s}{9}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{8s}{9})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9},\\,\\frac{8}{9}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-78404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{18},\\,\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{81},\\,\\frac{4}{81},\\,\\frac{8}{81}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{9}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9},\\,\\frac{8}{9}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9},\\,\\frac{8}{9}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨{t}^{2},\\,-2{t}^{2},\\,-2⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s={t}^{2},$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s={t}^{2},$ we have that $t=\\sqrt{s}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨{(\\sqrt{s})}^{2},\\,-2{(\\sqrt{s})}^{2},\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨s,\\,-2s,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parameterized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-127706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "T(s)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}+2,\\,3-{t}^{4}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}+2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-{t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,2{t}^{3},\\,-4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|2{t}^{3}|\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}\\sqrt{4+1+4} \\\\  & =6{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}6{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{t}{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{u}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}$ and $t\\ge 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4} & =s \\\\ {t}^{4} & =\\frac{2s}{3} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}}) \\\\  & =⟨{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4}+2,\\,3-{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2s}{3},\\,\\frac{s}{3}+2,\\,3-\\frac{2s}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-127739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨s,\\,2s+3,\\,2s-3⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨s,\\,2s-3,\\,-2s⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{4}⟨2s,\\,3s,\\,2-\\sqrt{3}\\,s⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{4}⟨3s,\\,s,\\,1-\\sqrt{6}\\,s⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78391" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4})\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4})\\,j,$  $\\,t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78391" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4}))i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4}))j \\\\  & =-4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4})\\,i+4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4})\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{[-4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4})]}^{2}+{[4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4})]}^{2}} \\\\  & =4|t{|}^{3}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡({t}^{4})+{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{4})} \\\\  & =4{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}4{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={u}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & ={t}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, since $s={t}^{4}$, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{4} & =s \\\\ t & =\\sqrt[4]{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt[4]{s}) \\\\  & =cos\\,((\\sqrt[4]{s})^{4})\\,i+sin\\,((\\sqrt[4]{s})^{4})\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78391" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-78391" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78391" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s)\\,j"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s)\\,j"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡({s}^{3})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({s}^{3})\\,j"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({s}^{4})\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({s}^{4})\\,j"] ["math" "{cos}^{4}⁡(s)\\,i+{sin}^{4}⁡(s)\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78391" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s)\\,j"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\frac{t}{2},\\,\\frac{t}{2},\\,t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\cdot u{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,t$,  we have that $t=\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s,\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-78390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{2},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6}⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{3}⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{8}⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{4},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{4},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{8}⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-78390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3,\\,t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =|t| \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2},$ we have that $t=\\sqrt{2s}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{2s}) \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s},\\,3,\\,\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-127723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "R(s)=⟨2s\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,\\,3,\\,-2s\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨2s\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,\\,3,\\,2s\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨\\frac{s}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,3,\\,\\frac{s}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s},\\,3,\\,-\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s},\\,3,\\,\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "R(s)=⟨\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s},\\,3,\\,\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127727" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127727" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{2({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s={e}^{t}-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}-1 & =s \\\\ {e}^{t} & =s+1 \\\\ t & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-(s+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127727" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "baf099d33e3d996a85aab7a62bd5dea044b4a0e2f1789074252a9a89d64e5879"} {"question" "q-127727" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127727" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s)⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s+1),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s+1)⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{s}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s-1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s-1)]⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s)⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "q-127727" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f908438e1a1a20a9c0de0a85a83ddd6512196997082ce154f252192c0590c00"} {"question" "e-3065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle 2t-1 ,\\: 8t+2 ,\\: -2t \\right\\rangle, \\, t \\geq 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf{r}(0)$ to $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ is given by $s=6\\sqrt{2}t.$ Find $\\mathbf R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/example-3065.json" "file_sha256" "3a9705038efb6202dca18c0a4e00b913da485edc9fa91156e420f502a11ccba9"} {"question" "e-3065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since  $s=6\\sqrt{2}t,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{2}t & =s \\\\ t & =\\frac{s}{6\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ t & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s \\geq 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}) \\\\  & =⟨2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})-1,\\,8(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})+2,\\,-2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}-1,\\,\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}s}{6}+2,\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨\\sqrt{2}s-6,\\,4\\sqrt{2}s+12,\\,-\\sqrt{2}s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/example-3065.json" "file_sha256" "3a9705038efb6202dca18c0a4e00b913da485edc9fa91156e420f502a11ccba9"} {"question" "e-3067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=\\cos{t}\\,\\mathbf i - \\sin{t}\\,\\mathbf j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,\\mathbf k, \\, t \\geq 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf r(0)$ to $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by $s=2t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $\\mathbf{T}(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/example-3067.json" "file_sha256" "10a2c4dcad41dff1ffebb60e63eef52420d90c737581ad67f0ab93a457e4d3fb"} {"question" "e-3067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s=2t,$ we have that $t=\\dfrac{s}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $\\mathbf R(s)$ that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{s}{2}k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s,$ the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}s}\\mathbf R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2})k \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\,k).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/example-3067.json" "file_sha256" "10a2c4dcad41dff1ffebb60e63eef52420d90c737581ad67f0ab93a457e4d3fb"} {"question" "e-3066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the parametrization of the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=2(t\\cos{t}-\\sin{t})\\,\\mathbf i+2(t\\sin{t}+\\cos{t})\\,\\mathbf j, \\, t \\geq 0$ by its arc length $s?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/example-3066.json" "file_sha256" "53290eafe925b04259f257ac74386dc93cdfc27e43d5621eb02a133b4b341b78"} {"question" "e-3066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and its magnitude $\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|2t|\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the last step, we removed the absolute value bars since $t>0.$ \n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}2u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={u}^{2}{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}-0 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $s=t^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =s \\\\ t & =\\pm \\sqrt{s} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt{s},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ntaking the positive root because $t>0.$  \n\nFinally, the vector function that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{s}) \\\\  & =2(\\sqrt{s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s})\\,i+2(\\sqrt{s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068638/example-3066.json" "file_sha256" "53290eafe925b04259f257ac74386dc93cdfc27e43d5621eb02a133b4b341b78"}] "usage" {"q-33860" [] "e-3066" [] "q-33861" [] "e-3065" [] "e-3067" []} "basis" 2308 "retractions" [[17592186120212 :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t) = ⟨2t, 1 - 3t, 5 + 6t⟩$, $t \\ge 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s = 7t$. Find $R(s)$, the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s$."] [17592186120213 :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t) = 8\\cos ti + 8\\sin tj + 6tk$, $t \\ge 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s = 10t$, find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s)$, parametrized by $s$."] [17592186119488 :question/problem "Consider the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle 2t-1,\\: 8t+2,\\: -2t \\right\\rangle, \\, t \\geq 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf{r}(0)$ to $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ is given by $s=6\\sqrt{2}t$. Find $\\mathbf R(s)$, the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s$."] [17592186119488 :question/worked-solution "First, since\n\n$$\ns=6\\sqrt{2}t\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6\\sqrt{2}t &= s \\\\\nt &= \\frac{s}{6\\sqrt{2}} \\\\\nt &= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length $s$, with\n\n$$\ns \\geq 0\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nR(s) &= r(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}) \\\\\n&= ⟨2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}) - 1, 8(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}) + 2,-2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6} - 1, \\frac{4\\sqrt{2}s}{6} + 2,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}⟨\\sqrt{2}s - 6, 4\\sqrt{2}s + 12,-\\sqrt{2}s⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119490 :question/problem "Given the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=\\cos{t}\\,\\mathbf i - \\sin{t}\\,\\mathbf j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,\\mathbf k, \\, t \\geq 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf r(0)$ to $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by $s=2t$, find the corresponding unit tangent $\\mathbf{T}(s)$, parametrized by $s$."] [17592186119490 :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=2t$, we have that\n\n$$\nt=\\dfrac{s}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $\\mathbf R(s)$ that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nR(s) &= r(\\frac{s}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\cos (\\frac{s}{2})i - \\sin (\\frac{s}{2})j + \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\frac{s}{2}k \\\\\n&= \\cos (\\frac{s}{2})i - \\sin (\\frac{s}{2})j + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2}k\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}s}\\mathbf R(s)\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT(s) &= \\frac{d}{ds}R(s) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{ds}(\\cos (\\frac{s}{2}))i + \\frac{d}{ds}(-\\sin (\\frac{s}{2}))j + \\frac{d}{ds}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2})k \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{s}{2})i - \\frac{1}{2}\\cos (\\frac{s}{2})j + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}k \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(-\\sin (\\frac{s}{2})i - \\cos (\\frac{s}{2})j + \\sqrt{3}k)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119489 :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=2(t\\cos{t}-\\sin{t})\\,\\mathbf i+2(t\\sin{t}+\\cos{t})\\,\\mathbf j, \\, t \\geq 0$ by its arc length $s$?"] [17592186119489 :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and its magnitude $\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{′}(t) &= 2\\frac{d}{dt}(t\\cos t - \\sin t)i + 2\\frac{d}{dt}(t\\sin t + \\cos t)j \\\\\n&= 2(\\cos t - t\\sin t - \\cos t)i + 2(\\sin t + t\\cos t - \\sin t)j \\\\\n&=-2t\\sin ti + 2t\\cos tj \\\\\n‖r^{′}(t)‖ &= \\mid 2t \\mid \\sqrt{(-\\sin t)^{2} + \\cos^{2} t} \\\\\n&= 2t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the last step, we removed the absolute value bars since $t>0$.\n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ns &= ∫_{0}^{t}‖r^{′}(u)‖du \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{t}2udu \\\\\n&= u^{2} \\mid _{0}^{t} \\\\\n&= t^{2} - 0 \\\\\n&= t^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $s=t^2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nt^{2} &= s \\\\\nt &= ± \\sqrt{s} \\\\\nt &= \\sqrt{s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ntaking the positive root because $t>0$.\n\nFinally, the vector function that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nR(s) &= r(\\sqrt{s}) \\\\\n&= 2(\\sqrt{s}\\cos \\sqrt{s} - \\sin \\sqrt{s})i + 2(\\sqrt{s}\\sin \\sqrt{s} + \\cos \\sqrt{s})j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186117773 17592186117774 17592186117775 17592186117776 17592186117777 17592186117779 17592186117780 17592186117781 17592186117782 17592186117783] "immutable_fields" [[17592186117772 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117772 :answer-field/id] [17592186117772 :answer-field/key] [17592186117772 :answer-field/type] [17592186117778 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117778 :answer-field/id] [17592186117778 :answer-field/key] [17592186117778 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
